CRASH-25: reject out-of-range flow unit codes in EN_setflowunits

EN_setflowunits stored any integer as the flow units code. initunits()
then used it to index RptFlowUnitsTxt[] (and saveinpfile FlowUnitsTxt[]),
reading past the end of the table, and an unknown code silently got the
CFS conversion factor. Return 251, as EN_init does for the same argument.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-25_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..9a1f04c 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -1482,6 +1482,7 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_setflowunits(EN_Project p, int units)
     double *Ucf = p->Ucf;
 
     if (!p->Openflag) return 102;
+    if (units < 0 || units > CMS) return 251;
 
     // Determine unit system based on flow units
     qfactor = Ucf[FLOW];
